  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "At a Senate Judiciary subcommittee hearing chaired by Sen. Josh Hawley, senators raised Fourth Amendment and privacy concerns about Flock Safety's nationwide ALPR network, hearing from a wrongly arrested Florida woman and Pinal County, Arizona Sheriff Ross Teeple, who ended his agency's Flock contract over unaddressed privacy concerns. Senators also discussed risks of tracking abortion seekers, gun-show attendees, and ICE access to Flock data.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "If you haven't heard of Flock, all I have to say is Flock's probably heard of you. I'm sure we're all in the database.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "I was trying to get answers from them, and they would not give me answers\u2026 and there were too many concerns. So we just decided not to continue our contract.",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    },
    {
      "quote": "In my case, a Flock camera captured my vehicle a few miles from the scene of a terrible crash. That piece of information became part of an investigation that ultimately led to my arrest on three counts of vehicular homicide and 13 days in jail for a crash I had nothing to do with.",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    }
  ],
